    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nConsolidated all duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId`, rejecting a create with **409** only when a new owner's *whole* identity key equals an existing owner's.\n\n**`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getIdentityKey()` that builds the key from the stored E.164 telephone, lower-cased email (empty when absent/blank), and `householdId` (empty when not sharing a household).\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n- Replaced the three separate checks (`isTelephoneInUse` \u2192 `DuplicateTelephoneException`, `isEmailInUse` \u2192 `DuplicateEmailException`, `isHouseholdInUse` \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException`) with a single `isIdentityKeyInUse(owner.getIdentityKey())` check that throws `DuplicateIdentityException`.\n- The new owner's `householdId` is now assigned *before* the check (via `householdIdFor`), so the key reflects the final household segment. `joinHousehold` was split into a pure `backfillHousehold(...)` that only back-fills existing members after the checks pass.\n- Removed the three unused helpers and imports.\n\n**`advice/`** \u2014 added `DuplicateIdentityException` (409) and its handler; deleted the three now-unused exception classes and their handlers.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct auto-maps `getIdentityKey()` \u2192 the response (verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`).\n\n## Behavioural effect\n- Two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with **different telephones** now produce different keys and are both allowed.\n- Same email or same last-name/address alone no longer triggers a 409 \u2014 only an exact full-key match does.\n\n## Tests\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / **BUILD SUCCESS**. The debug log confirms owner `b` (same telephone, empty email/household \u2192 key `+61400000004||`) was rejected as a conflict.",
